# One language per reply

- If the user writes in Hebrew, reply entirely in Hebrew.
- If the user writes in English, reply entirely in English.
- Never mix Hebrew and English in the same sentence or the same message.
- Do not translate mid-sentence. Do not sandwich English technical narration inside Hebrew, or Hebrew inside English.
- File paths, URLs, code identifiers, and proper names stay as-is; surrounding prose stays in the chosen language.
